================================================================================
DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI BatteryDegradationPage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure
@Observable state holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) exposing loading/empty/error/success over
an injectable dual-source BatteryDegradationDataSource seam (primary health analytics drives the phase;
the degradation source is independent, web's separate query) whose value types mirror the KMP
BatteryHealthAnalytics / DegradationData wire shape 1:1. The page reproduces the web chrome
(title/subtitle/VehicleSelect), the four summary MetricCards, the SOH RadialGauge + band badge, the
prediction panel (natural-language "reaches 80% in ~N years" sentence + four sub-metrics, or the
need-more-data callout), the health-trend projection (ChartContainer + a native Swift-Charts ComposedChart
port: actual/projected lines + 95% confidence bounds + 80%/70% references), the range-loss AreaChart, the
scored risk-factor gauges, the recommendations list, the charging-impact AlertBanner, the three
battery-health-factor cards, and the sortable five-column degradation-history DataTable — all from the P2
tokens + P3 shared components (no hand-rolled glass, no direct Charts/recharts). Every data source
implements loading/empty/error/success and every section its own empty state; every visible string
resolves from Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names (64 keys added); SI kilometres/watt-hours
convert only at the render boundary via the shared Units facade; adaptive macOS/iPad vs iPhone-compact
layout (ADR-002/006). Verified GREEN on BOTH idioms by isolated Swift 6 strict-concurrency type-checks
(macOS 0 / iOS 0 errors in any Battery file) and an executed model+derivation+format harness (42/42),
plus swiftlint --strict (0), swiftformat --lint (0), and the placeholder gate (0). The full xcodebuild
scheme is RED ONLY due to one pre-existing, out-of-scope shared-surfaces ViewBuilder-return error
(Input.Previews.swift — forbidden to commit-fix), with ZERO diagnostics in any of my files.

